# Cases a VM run may report skipped, as `case: reason` (format: e2e/check-cases.sh). Everything in cases.list can run in a VM, and
# check-cases.sh refuses fallback-tpmbound-*, upgrade-kinds-tpmbound and tpm-kind-* skipped in a VM run whatever this file says. The vm-silent-* cases need an encrypted-tpm import:
# only the lacking mode runs them (refused skipped there, whatever this file says); the full mode reports them skipped.
vm-silent-import-fails: full mode: an RSA import goes to tpm, so a missing libtss2-rc cannot make it fail; the case needs the lacking mode
vm-silent-journal-cause: full mode: an RSA import goes to tpm, so a missing libtss2-rc cannot make it fail; the case needs the lacking mode
vm-silent-nothing-stored: full mode: an RSA import goes to tpm, so a missing libtss2-rc cannot make it fail; the case needs the lacking mode
vm-silent-no-key: full mode: an RSA import goes to tpm, so a missing libtss2-rc cannot make it fail; the case needs the lacking mode
vm-silent-restored-imports: full mode: an RSA import goes to tpm, so a missing libtss2-rc cannot make it fail; the case needs the lacking mode
snap-record: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-socket-dir: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-list-keys: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-sign-rsa: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-sign-ec: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-polkit-per-signature: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-journal-label: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-bus-denied: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-refused-unconfined: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-refused-root: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-refused-other-snap: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
snap-unknown-methods: lacking mode: the snap group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC Design 6); the route does not depend on the TPM kind
vm-fingerprint-stage: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-polkit-finger: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-polkit-unenrolled: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-polkit-timeout: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-sudo: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-negative: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-disabled: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-sign: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-fallback-module: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-fallback-daemon: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-fallback-reader: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-fingerprint-fallback-finger: lacking mode: the fingerprint group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC, end-to-end scope; acceptances 18 and 19)
vm-memory-swap-max: lacking mode: the memory group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC acceptance 24); the unit, the kernel and the handlers do not depend on the TPM mode
vm-memory-default-stage: lacking mode: the memory group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC acceptance 24); the unit, the kernel and the handlers do not depend on the TPM mode
vm-memory-default-crash: lacking mode: the memory group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC acceptance 24); the unit, the kernel and the handlers do not depend on the TPM mode
vm-memory-default-crash-override: lacking mode: the memory group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC acceptance 24); the unit, the kernel and the handlers do not depend on the TPM mode
vm-memory-default-control: lacking mode: the memory group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC acceptance 24); the unit, the kernel and the handlers do not depend on the TPM mode
vm-memory-coredump-stage: lacking mode: the memory group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC acceptance 24); the unit, the kernel and the handlers do not depend on the TPM mode
vm-memory-coredump-crash: lacking mode: the memory group runs in the full VM mode (SPEC acceptance 24); the unit, the kernel and the handlers do not depend on the TPM mode
